Title: Artificial intelligence-enabled early intracranial volumetric response predicts systemic progression-free survival in the phase III CROWN study.
Abstract: Manual endpoint assessment is labor-intensive and variable. This study evaluated artificial intelligence (AI)-powered intracranial response assessment and explored imaging prognostic factors in the phase III CROWN trial of advanced treatment-naive anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK)-positive non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC).

