Title: Heterogeneity of thromboembolic risk across ALK inhibitors: a retrospective real-world study identifying crizotinib-specific signals and high-risk subpopulations.
Abstract: Patients with anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK)-positive malignancies increasingly rely on ALK inhibitors (ALKis) as first-line therapy, yet thromboembolism (TE) across the ALKi family and its impact on patients' safety remain incompletely characterized, particularly in the real-world populations.

